#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3106e82a-12db-54bf-bcfb-7f996ea074ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3106e82a-12db-54bf-bcfb-7f996ea074ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702982} :answer-field/id #uuid "a44533f1-d725-51c5-a7ba-9c52eb9a7caf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4330f45-25a5-589a-90b5-ca75a331435a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4330f45-25a5-589a-90b5-ca75a331435a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702999} :answer-field/id #uuid "db3a44fe-3ca0-5c15-b4e8-99c757d30983" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186702997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4d97cd5-dc50-548d-be43-42ef67d6f00d" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle x,0,1\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle 0,2,0\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=2 \\sqrt{17}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nUse the determinant setup\n\n$$\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\x&0&1\\\\0&2&0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRecall that the magnitude of $\\langle u,v,w\\rangle$ is $\\sqrt{u^2+v^2+w^2}$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, compute each signed component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\x&0&1\\\\0&2&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nc_1&=\\begin{vmatrix}0&1\\\\2&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((0)(0)-(1)(2))=-2\\\\\nc_2&=-\\begin{vmatrix}x&1\\\\0&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=-((x)(0)-(1)(0))=0\\\\\nc_3&=\\begin{vmatrix}x&0\\\\0&2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((x)(2)-(0)(0))=2x\\\\\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\langle -2,0,2x\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $N(x)$ be the sum of the squared components. Compute the magnitude, square both sides, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(x)&=(-2)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(0)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(2x)^2\\\\\n&=4x^{2} + 4\\\\\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{4x^{2} + 4}\\\\\n\\sqrt{4x^{2} + 4}&=2 \\sqrt{17}\\\\\n4x^{2} + 4&=68\\\\\n4x^2&=64\\\\\nx^2&=16\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt{16}\\\\\nx&=-4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck each candidate in the squared magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(-4)&=68=68\\\\\nN(4)&=68=68\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $N(x)$ is the sum of the squared cross-product components. Both magnitudes are nonnegative, so these checks also verify the original magnitude equation. In ascending order, all real solutions are $x=-4$ and $x=4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e485cb1-e041-541b-b309-795aff3e641a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e485cb1-e041-541b-b309-795aff3e641a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703012} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fe5acc7-2fd1-566e-863d-fa68d867af41" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703013} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1017aca4-b41b-55bf-967c-686bebb352f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd3800cb9eb7ccc1642b041b4c336fc3567f0891825b00f169da4fec9d3cbed6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703006} {:answer/id #uuid "375d6935-9061-5505-b3d4-69f78cf8d1ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/29/29ac743d73164f7868c83ca644f6c04d6d233d336ffffbbe13ab060b834786dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703016} {:answer/id #uuid "3792ec2d-0749-5198-ab21-6ab97c732f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a4/a4c04ef27ffb0af9273091a0be426a81db61454c1c5ac20c4acc0d1f85795299.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703017} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4165f0-5afc-5257-a245-a18c1f2fa496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/546d3b588a7661eb7728d5c2f5693a8ef2c868ab486bcb677fd9133157ce6fec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703033} {:answer/id #uuid "b12b59fe-af52-5fb0-9230-51e48ab3d36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/60/60f215a1bcb5bcc6f7d384d1c98f667e58d3126a72b47ee21d05d2c3f161c018.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "375d6935-9061-5505-b3d4-69f78cf8d1ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/29/29ac743d73164f7868c83ca644f6c04d6d233d336ffffbbe13ab060b834786dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703016} :answer-field/id #uuid "463be4c0-1dc7-519f-8d65-106691bc9b88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703020} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94c631ba-fd0a-56d7-aecf-dccd618e6fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94c631ba-fd0a-56d7-aecf-dccd618e6fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703034} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa9282c-d016-5785-b177-63f965910af0" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "20378425-c645-5de8-a465-dad10c118b55" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=-x-1$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-2$ and $x=1$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-2$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=1$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x-1 \\\\  & =-(-2)-1 \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-2,1).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x-1 \\\\  & =-(1)-1 \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,-2).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-x-1.$\n\n![](images/28/2872e56343d018e4b0b1abb42632e3ebfb7b623108535564afe4af1ca86d976b.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703010 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f62f68ab-338e-5b41-bc2b-1499bf181e34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f62f68ab-338e-5b41-bc2b-1499b