t, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1+\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\  & =1+0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,1).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-4.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1+\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{2}(-4) \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(-4,-1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=1+\\frac{1}{2}x.$\n\n![](images/ec/ec1e2afb0ca460fabf39276605226cbc17078fe92ff79704d4ddf1ce08a9f593.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edee8932-f3f1-54c7-ba0b-bfd07baacddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edee8932-f3f1-54c7-ba0b-bfd07baacddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703149} :answer-field/id #uuid "575045b0-95a0-5efe-bfc8-111cdd8b952b" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d85a3ad-912b-51e1-8ec8-be5fab003630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d85a3ad-912b-51e1-8ec8-be5fab003630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703105} :answer-field/id #uuid "c548eb11-2e32-523b-b9d9-8d8f2801e470" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type 