d} :question/id #uuid "29952585-14a7-579a-9b92-fe412e971cca" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=-2x+1$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-2$ and $x=1$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-2$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=1$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+1 \\\\  & =-2(-2)+1 \\\\  & =4+1 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-2,5).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+1 \\\\  & =-2(1)+1 \\\\  & =-2+1 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,-1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-2x+1.$\n\n![](images/ff/ff833dec09278cf2f9ad1d6642246e53f67a3a2a0352e6c016e6a7c888f0da16.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db620a1a-f145-504b-bcff-279d4241e81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db620a1a-f145-504b-bcff-279d4241e81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703144} :answer-field/id #uuid "4eec4ee9-5918-5ada-8c8a-2757b6f272f6" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011d164c-0323-59ae-8791-6ed979534e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045