d #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703133} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1657af9-2039-5bd4-9a4a-a1b378a697a0" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90e9cce6-032f-5e29-a7b9-412ce297edad" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-3$ and $x=6$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-3$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=6$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-3.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{3}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-3) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-3,-1).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=6.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{3}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(6,2).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{3}x.$ \n\n![](images/a7/a7ee4360ef9e4466005d2ff3652357f804c057a4645653eaafde9adf2dc5886f.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822fb939-68da-587c-8799-08499e09df0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "822fb939-68da-587c-8799-08499e09df0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703120} :answer-field/id #uuid "e78425b5-e30f-59bd-bc4b-5821dcab4601" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee804d58-fc97-539b-aa8c-4fcf37275619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee804d58-fc97-539b-aa8c-4fcf37275619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703150} :answer-field/id #uuid "f28a9c22-2055-5ebc-adcb-634937fcad9c" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8278d77f-e4e2-5e74-b4ab-cdeb38ba0950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c8/c891b97111decfd2e2d58623cc24db4174d794f012de4f00c59d017b28fa265b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703121} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6d85ea-4d77-5d49-984d-8a3ffbf79d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/06/06cf0c51a2d6a03f1ce7ab4434774b3f281e4c280546541a45f78a15e2e08bcd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703124} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c497ce-88ff-5d15-88d9-842bf6faeadd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1c/1c38f92ee450a08555763715b866d8d757f24329d8b173c412f1e28c93248c42.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703130} {:answer/id #uuid "a2e6afb4-cc31-55fa-8f41-54a64f36f42b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/501a7d9f43ee0727cdb2dd6b9ce3fd75c0814fda92e56d88c7f621b770b07192.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703131} {:answer/id #uuid "d833afc7-8149-5ca5-b724-3df84eab7eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/71/717afcde0b8ded7f6c94197b87de4901525d9b34f6106852806f82b8da64a765.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1c497ce-88ff-5d15-88d9-842bf6faeadd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1c/1c38f92ee450a08555763715b866d8d757f24329d8b173c412f1e28c93248c42.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703130} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe344519-2373-5425-881e-bca9d8478867" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "98ee99ad-8b01-5a88-b529-79dbcb9c5e21" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=1-\\frac{1}{2}x$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-4$ and $x=2$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-4$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=2$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-4.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1-\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2}(-4) \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-4,3).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1-\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2}(2) \\\\  & =1-1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,0).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=1-\\frac{1}{2}x.$\n\n![](images/2d/2d4a9de0be8d3619a976daa775f9cbd56ecbd1a43a400ac573d67464db3e62eb.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29848274-0851-522f-8c45-7a63340416ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29848274-0851-522f-8c45-7a63340416ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703108} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ceae919-7465-58b0-ae87-b535b458982f" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a0438ab-e7d9-58b2-85e3-e718ef7efe2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a0438ab-e7d9-58b2-85e3-e718ef7efe2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703119} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b89970-18bf-54a8-b4ea-f22857544ad2" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703129} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0746d7e9-aee3-5a69-af8c-fbede2311e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8c353c411299420f50fef1bd9bbe6391b16dfe9cdbb61bf655becd41d8431df2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703103} {:answer/id #uuid "273073ad-afe7-576a-b5b2-578db4643f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/930ab140366898b219de63fd5acb6379891e39108eb4d4ea7a54ae4c2d4d558b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703107} {:answer/id #uuid "3ae9e578-8ff8-597f-855f-eaa85ba08d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/091bc1230b8729d0468ad940937d64dd89b04ae25d82615c8225157e1d191d18.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703113} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8cde23-1101-5000-85ec-7238107b0cca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c4a491847b4a6b647032831e563fe7d4007e63fb5dd4b594dd825c1055a82451.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703115} {:answer/id #uuid "e9fec37a-e174-594e-b149-a2affda72421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f6c613ac31220b890d69fb2db001c126fb49d04621c3641d0848973db9954069.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9fec37a-e174-594e-b149-a2affda72421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f6c613ac31220b890d69fb2db001c126fb49d04621c3641d0848973db9954069.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703148} :answer-field/id #uuid "adb45cbd-04d5-5f7e-9be7-ccb47ac018c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d395f198-1f72-513c-8b93-e0652a00ef12" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=2x-1$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-1$ and $x=1$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-1$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=1$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x-1 \\\\  & =2(-1)-1 \\\\  & =-2-1 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-1,-3).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x-1 \\\\  & =2(1)-1 \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=2x-1.$\n\n![](images/4c/4cb2d4bfae77b9d980d11ccb56c8ef32e3e0abb6418d1aee8e4053c0cc2021c7.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703155 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f859b0-6955-5742-95e5-35c512a6534a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a6/a606aab4d7579937d4c6f121fe506eddf1642073d848ac7e77d36fafc088fc66.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703106} {:answer/id #uuid "31c0e00f-0a17-5662-ab6e-b70b684ea4f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4b/4bbcfcaf2b07874f1e4480d3a0cb1571c2b9dae5e2651b8646eac4f5a21c28d7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703110} {:answer/id #uuid "38001e81-69e8-543c-aa41-a0268de85c95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f5ffabd6c2a8318c7275ed643e1b7e4bf7b41287549034f290ca88121b672475.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703111} {:answer/id #uuid "8d1174d0-aed3-5233-84ed-4ef2b52fdf9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1f/1f485f883bb45d4eb8f88846dadc64b5b97c923ab990f1c14e3f6122ddc779db.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703123} {:answer/id #uuid "dbaed7f2-3124-5b63-9971-8233143d9a9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/88/88f3274e669b5256758247ef1f5ec00082d9c26fdaeafcc026d0b91f0af754b1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f859b0-6955-5742-95e5-35c512a6534a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a6/a606aab4d7579937d4c6f121fe506eddf1642073d848ac7e77d36fafc088fc66.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703106} :answer-field/id #uuid "cda7c12b-c288-5d96-86a2-1a49dab9b9a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703139} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4cbd440-d525-5b68-82df-16dcaa7980fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4cbd440-d525-5b68-82df-16dcaa7980fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703137} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5ba86b5-3420-541d-b810-8dbedec9f9fb" :answer-field/key "point-first" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703142} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3845c610-4d52-594e-8d34-c46707a1aca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3845c610-4d52-594e-8d34-c46707a1aca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703112} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8b6f0bc-fddb-586b-97e3-ac89613a9c65" :answer-field/key "point-second" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff323cca-63af-5e8a-8a0b-4865df7a9696" :question/problem "Which graph shows the line $y=-x$?\n\nFirst give the two points on this line with $x=-2$ and $x=1$. Enter each answer as an ordered pair $(x,y)$, then select the graph.\n\nPoint with $x=-2$: {{point-first}}\n\nPoint with $x=1$: {{point-second}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(-2,2).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x \\\\  & =-(1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,-1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-x.$ \n\n![](images/32/32ebf89997d1dd0f10e20cc086c36ca5462819b3625a00d15e8ae98a023a4651.png)\n\nAll choices have the same $y$-intercept. Check another point to distinguish the lines."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703816 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29ba056f-dc7a-5ec0-9d71-4c4ad220dd96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703817} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7cdedf-39d7-51ad-a71a-218e090943a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 1}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703818} {:answer/id #uuid "a2b50c68-8c31-5758-ac80-c224742d5268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{- x^{2} + 1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703824} {:answer/id #uuid "cac14fed-f2a4-516d-bd24-05bf370ede9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 1}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703828} {:answer/id #uuid "d47609b1-7bd5-511c-8351-d07ab1e8ff83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c7cdedf-39d7-51ad-a71a-218e090943a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 1}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703818} :answer-field/id #uuid "688c0c6f-f675-5fc3-ac9d-ec2a9d1434e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2871584c-4c28-59aa-8d48-c20dea677b2f" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\sin t,\\qquad y=\\cot t,\\qquad 0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx=\\sin t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\sin t=x \\\\\ny=\\cot t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\cot t=y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t & =1 \\\\\n\\cos^2 t & =1-\\sin^2 t \\\\\n\\cos t & =\\sqrt{1-\\sin^2 t}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe used here that $\\cos t>0$ in the range $0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$\n\nNow, using the definition of a cotangent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\cot t=\\frac{\\cos t}{\\sin t}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-\\sin^2 t}}{\\sin t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sin t=x$ and $\\cot t=y$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 1}}{x}.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 1}}{x}.$\n\nThe traced curve also satisfies $0<x<1\\quad y>0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703823 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5935f8ce-061d-5ca3-9a13-0cf09f9f34a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{x^{2} + 4}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703819} {:answer/id #uuid "6fcc0507-b7fc-54c9-8794-453e52112886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4 x}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703821} {:answer/id #uuid "796ae06a-6527-5749-8ce8-c7371c244f2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{x^{2} + 4}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703822} {:answer/id #uuid "a401fd39-7140-57f0-9736-0fd9e365f7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703825} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a8914d-5554-5eb9-a24b-4fb17e1b1e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a401fd39-7140-57f0-9736-0fd9e365f7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703825} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4b47b96-c95f-5231-acc5-5476ab0ace94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91fb0096-905c-5784-af6f-c7549377cbc5" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\cos t,\\qquad y=2\\tan t,\\qquad 0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx=2\\cos t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\cos t=\\frac{x}{2} \\\\\ny=2\\tan t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\tan t=\\frac{y}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t & =1 \\\\\n\\sin^2 t & =1-\\cos^2 t \\\\\n\\sin t & =\\sqrt{1-\\cos^2 t}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe used here that $\\sin t>0$ in the range $0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$\n\nNow, using the definition of a tangent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\tan t=\\frac{\\sin t}{\\cos t}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-\\cos^2 t}}{\\cos t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\cos t=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $\\tan t=\\frac{y}{2}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive. Substituting this root and cancelling the common scale gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2}}{\\frac{x}{2}} \\\\\ny & =\\frac{2 \\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}{x}.$\n\nThe traced curve also satisfies $0<x<2\\quad y>0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa4ff85b-021d-5ae2-895b-e0ef55c36f2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703826} {:answer/id #uuid "d5fc4a94-495c-54ad-b81e-4f5e9e81fff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703830} {:answer/id #uuid "d69261f8-3cc3-5075-b66d-080fdc3767dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4 \\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703831} {:answer/id #uuid "f9ceb026-3517-5642-8513-fd89adccf039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + 4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703834} {:answer/id #uuid "fa702d32-e7f5-5336-a7cb-b0011e7c282c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + 4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa4ff85b-021d-5ae2-895b-e0ef55c36f2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703826} :answer-field/id #uuid "071a9e5b-3384-54a5-9ba9-6d611b0be237" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba28be53-40e7-5b1e-9f9f-9a74be3a30f5" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\sin t,\\qquad y=2\\tan t,\\qquad 0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx=2\\sin t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\sin t=\\frac{x}{2} \\\\\ny=2\\tan t & \\Rightarrow\\quad \\tan t=\\frac{y}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t & =1 \\\\\n\\cos^2 t & =1-\\sin^2 t \\\\\n\\cos t & =\\sqrt{1-\\sin^2 t}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe used here that $\\cos t>0$ in the range $0<t<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$\n\nNow, using the definition of a tangent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\tan t=\\frac{\\sin t}{\\cos t}=\\frac{\\sin t}{\\sqrt{1-\\sin^2 t}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sin t=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $\\tan t=\\frac{y}{2}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive. Substituting this root and cancelling the common scale gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{\\frac{x}{2}}{\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2}} \\\\\ny & =\\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{- x^{2} + 4}}.$\n\nThe traced curve also satisfies $0<x<2\\quad y>0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703942 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd4f428-2054-5e60-810c-ab135978eb15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 4 x - 2}{9 x + 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cd4f428-2054-5e60-810c-ab135978eb15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 4 x - 2}{9 x + 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703943} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da118a6-0f34-5204-a7f0-78bafec7a27c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703946} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b38a42ef-e061-5d63-b3b2-6f802989b6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b38a42ef-e061-5d63-b3b2-6f802989b6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703949} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac5a49ce-3366-5f64-a922-1a28fe1a428f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2701513f-19c5-512b-b879-0ac0465ac508" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{t - 4},\\quad y=- \\frac{t}{2 t + 1},\\quad t\\ne - \\frac{1}{2},\\quad t\\ne 4.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation is\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}$,\\quad x\\ne 0,\\quad x\\ne$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Eliminate the parameter by using the $x$ equation to isolate $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x &=\\frac{2}{t - 4} \\\\ t &=4 + \\frac{2}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=4 + \\frac{2}{x}$ into the original $y$ expression, then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=-\\left(\\frac{(4 + \\frac{2}{x})}{2 (4 + \\frac{2}{x}) + 1}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{4 + \\frac{2}{x}}{9 + \\frac{4}{x}} \\\\ &=\\frac{(-4 - \\frac{2}{x})(x)}{(9 + \\frac{4}{x})(x)} \\\\ &=- \\frac{2 (2 x + 1)}{9 x + 4} \\\\ &=\\frac{- 4 x - 2}{9 x + 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reciprocal $x$ expression never equals $0$. The other excluded parameter value $t=- \\frac{1}{2}$ would give $x=- \\frac{4}{9}$, so it must also be excluded. The simplified formula alone does not retain every missing point.\n\nTherefore the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{- 4 x - 2}{9 x + 4},\\quad x\\ne - \\frac{4}{9},\\quad x\\ne 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78f1d09d-e7ec-5b29-8eee-3af136884365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x + 2}{7 x + 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78f1d09d-e7ec-5b29-8eee-3af136884365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x + 2}{7 x + 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703944} :answer-field/id #uuid "95f7e7cd-989f-5f3e-b510-bb58dc629e09" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703947} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb5aae48-070f-5e92-9cc6-eb3f5d1d2613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb5aae48-070f-5e92-9cc6-eb3f5d1d2613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703951} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e3600c-ac6e-55d5-9031-1f3167c62d44" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "898a649a-895d-50d6-a08e-ed9327b12610" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=- \\frac{2}{t + 3},\\quad y=- \\frac{t}{1 - 2 t},\\quad t\\ne -3,\\quad t\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation is\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}$,\\quad x\\ne 0,\\quad x\\ne$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Eliminate the parameter by using the $x$ equation to isolate $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x &=- \\frac{2}{t + 3} \\\\ t &=-3 - \\frac{2}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $t=-3 - \\frac{2}{x}$ into the original $y$ expression, then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &=-\\left(\\frac{(-3 - \\frac{2}{x})}{1 - 2 (-3 - \\frac{2}{x})}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{-3 - \\frac{2}{x}}{7 + \\frac{4}{x}} \\\\ &=\\frac{(3 + \\frac{2}{x})(x)}{(7 + \\frac{4}{x})(x)} \\\\ &=- \\frac{- 3 x - 2}{7 x + 4} \\\\ &=\\frac{3 x + 2}{7 x + 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reciprocal $x$ expression never equals $0$. The other excluded parameter value $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ would give $x=- \\frac{4}{7}$, so it must also be excluded. The simplified formula alone does not retain every missing point.\n\nTherefore the complete Cartesian equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3 x + 2}{7 x + 4},\\quad x\\ne - \\frac{4}{7},\\quad x\\ne 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703952 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "091eba36-61b0-5312-a3ff-f5379d10311e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703955} {:answer/id #uuid "10ad0ded-1a71-564e-aa4c-fdce2ead39b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703957} {:answer/id #uuid "8e857a9d-1c1e-5441-b18d-84321461813b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\mathbf i-\\,\\mathbf j-3\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703965} {:answer/id #uuid "c7887833-056f-5535-b48e-c9642a16c3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\mathbf i+\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703970} {:answer/id #uuid "f5078c7d-1fee-580b-a11c-10bda09faae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\mathbf i+\\,\\mathbf j-3\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "091eba36-61b0-5312-a3ff-f5379d10311e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703955} :answer-field/id #uuid "27242b27-eec1-583c-bd8b-28e77620cfb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0136f0d6-978a-5578-9405-0e52ef2434e5" :question/problem "Given the vector field\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(x,y,z)&=-\\bigl(x y^{2} + 2 y z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad-\\bigl(x^{2} y - x z^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j \\\\ &\\quad-\\bigl(2 x y + 2 x z + y^{2} z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(1,1,-1)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The middle cofactor is negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ \\partial/\\partial x&\\partial/\\partial y&\\partial/\\partial z \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nTake the cross partial derivatives, holding the other coordinates constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=\\bigl(- 2 x - 2 y z\\bigr)-\\bigl(2 x z\\bigr) \\\\ &=- 2 x z - 2 x - 2 y z \\\\ P_z-R_x&=\\bigl(- 2 y\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 2 y - 2 z\\bigr) \\\\ &=2 z \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=\\bigl(- 2 x y + z^{2}\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 2 x y - 2 z\\bigr) \\\\ &=z^{2} + 2 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F&=-\\bigl(2 x z + 2 x + 2 y z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad+2 z\\,\\mathbf j \\\\ &\\quad+\\bigl(z^{2} + 2 z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point into these derivatives, not into the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=- 2 (1) (-1) - 2 (1) - 2 (1) (-1) \\\\ &=2 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=2 (-1) \\\\ &=-2 \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=(-1)^{2} + 2 (-1) \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(1,1,-1)=2\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "059e5441-029f-572c-ab00-b2c7da2ea546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703954} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf595fa-c128-5050-a050-eec19f9933b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,\\mathbf i-12\\,\\mathbf j-6\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703960} {:answer/id #uuid "77660db0-6fc4-50cd-9ae0-59ad62405f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\mathbf i+\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703964} {:answer/id #uuid "ae941963-73c3-588c-8deb-30e745df90ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\mathbf i+12\\,\\mathbf j+6\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703966} {:answer/id #uuid "d8006274-e185-571b-bb3d-df26a59e6530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\mathbf i-\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf595fa-c128-5050-a050-eec19f9933b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,\\mathbf i-12\\,\\mathbf j-6\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703960} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceba069a-f4a7-5018-9241-0c1037b3b11c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0aa1adb7-fe7f-5696-ac2e-7ab7c13f2203" :question/problem "Given the vector field\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(x,y,z)&=-\\bigl(x z^{2} + 2 y^{2} z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad+\\bigl(2 x^{2} y + 2 x z - y z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j \\\\ &\\quad+\\bigl(x^{2} z - 2 x y\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(0,-2,1)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The middle cofactor is negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ \\partial/\\partial x&\\partial/\\partial y&\\partial/\\partial z \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nTake the cross partial derivatives, holding the other coordinates constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=\\bigl(- 2 x\\bigr)-\\bigl(2 x - y\\bigr) \\\\ &=- 4 x + y \\\\ P_z-R_x&=\\bigl(- 2 x z - 2 y^{2}\\bigr)-\\bigl(2 x z - 2 y\\bigr) \\\\ &=- 4 x z - 2 y^{2} + 2 y \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=\\bigl(4 x y + 2 z\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 4 y z\\bigr) \\\\ &=4 x y + 4 y z + 2 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F&=-\\bigl(4 x - y\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad-\\bigl(4 x z + 2 y^{2} - 2 y\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j \\\\ &\\quad+\\bigl(4 x y + 4 y z + 2 z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point into these derivatives, not into the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=- 4 (0) + (-2) \\\\ &=-2 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=- 4 (0) (1) - 2 (-2)^{2} + 2 (-2) \\\\ &=-12 \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=4 (0) (-2) + 4 (-2) (1) + 2 (1) \\\\ &=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(0,-2,1)=-2\\,\\mathbf i-12\\,\\mathbf j-6\\,\\mathbf k\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703962 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52287001-42a3-599a-aebc-f31abc7e6ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\mathbf i+32\\,\\mathbf j+16\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703961} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd489a7-7457-52c2-9b8b-6873323055e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16\\,\\mathbf i-24\\,\\mathbf j-32\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703963} {:answer/id #uuid "dedf591c-5cef-5803-99ed-7bf13b279483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\mathbf i+24\\,\\mathbf j+32\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703975} {:answer/id #uuid "ee505a35-c8b0-5ac8-b71e-c9b3dff117e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36\\,\\mathbf i+12\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703976} {:answer/id #uuid "f7893494-e580-56af-aaef-2a413cc300b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,\\mathbf i-4\\,\\mathbf j+12\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee505a35-c8b0-5ac8-b71e-c9b3dff117e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36\\,\\mathbf i+12\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703976} :answer-field/id #uuid "b73032ad-e6ad-5cea-a8f8-fa10afe955bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "56a6e1c7-d178-573b-867d-44dda6e09783" :question/problem "Given the vector field\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(x,y,z)&=-\\bigl(x y^{2} + 2 y z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad-\\bigl(x^{2} y + 2 x z^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j \\\\ &\\quad+\\bigl(2 x y - 2 x z + 2 y^{2} z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(-2,-2,2)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The middle cofactor is negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ \\partial/\\partial x&\\partial/\\partial y&\\partial/\\partial z \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nTake the cross partial derivatives, holding the other coordinates constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=\\bigl(2 x + 4 y z\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 4 x z\\bigr) \\\\ &=4 x z + 2 x + 4 y z \\\\ P_z-R_x&=\\bigl(- 2 y\\bigr)-\\bigl(2 y - 2 z\\bigr) \\\\ &=- 4 y + 2 z \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=\\bigl(- 2 x y - 2 z^{2}\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 2 x y - 2 z\\bigr) \\\\ &=- 2 z^{2} + 2 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F&=\\bigl(4 x z + 2 x + 4 y z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad-\\bigl(4 y - 2 z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j \\\\ &\\quad-\\bigl(2 z^{2} - 2 z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point into these derivatives, not into the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=4 (-2) (2) + 2 (-2) + 4 (-2) (2) \\\\ &=-36 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=- 4 (-2) + 2 (2) \\\\ &=12 \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=- 2 (2)^{2} + 2 (2) \\\\ &=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(-2,-2,2)=-36\\,\\mathbf i+12\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b6282cb-fb4a-5498-afaf-46335ccde8b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703959} {:answer/id #uuid "b69a7a49-b6db-521a-b7e4-4ee2b2da002e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703968} {:answer/id #uuid "cf98d8c6-ac5b-53f6-b6cc-e41927f7a6e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\mathbf i+4\\,\\mathbf j-8\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703972} {:answer/id #uuid "dc465d68-db08-5428-8af5-eb62ed9d9971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16\\,\\mathbf i-4\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703974} {:answer/id #uuid "f03a53cd-01b1-539d-b34d-fdcfd6d1f168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f03a53cd-01b1-539d-b34d-fdcfd6d1f168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703977} :answer-field/id #uuid "052e7abe-250b-5d56-bed7-2d74ccbab45c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "af174d81-22f7-5aa3-a083-d260e862ed06" :question/problem "Given the vector field\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(x,y,z)&=-\\bigl(2 x y + 2 x z^{2} + 2 y z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad+\\bigl(2 x z + 2 y z^{2}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j \\\\ &\\quad+\\bigl(x^{2} y + 2 y^{2} z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(0,2,-1)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The middle cofactor is negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ \\partial/\\partial x&\\partial/\\partial y&\\partial/\\partial z \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nTake the cross partial derivatives, holding the other coordinates constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=\\bigl(x^{2} + 4 y z\\bigr)-\\bigl(2 x + 4 y z\\bigr) \\\\ &=x^{2} - 2 x \\\\ P_z-R_x&=\\bigl(- 4 x z - 2 y\\bigr)-\\bigl(2 x y\\bigr) \\\\ &=- 2 x y - 4 x z - 2 y \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=\\bigl(2 z\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 2 x - 2 z\\bigr) \\\\ &=2 x + 4 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F&=\\bigl(x^{2} - 2 x\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad-\\bigl(2 x y + 4 x z + 2 y\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j \\\\ &\\quad+\\bigl(2 x + 4 z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point into these derivatives, not into the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=(0)^{2} - 2 (0) \\\\ &=0 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=- 2 (0) (2) - 4 (0) (-1) - 2 (2) \\\\ &=-4 \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=2 (0) + 4 (-1) \\\\ &=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(0,2,-1)=-4\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This uses $Q_y-P_x$, with the differentiation variables interchanged." :answer/id #uuid "1c709262-65f4-59d1-939c-37b4a6969c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{8}{3} + 8 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704503} {:answer/feedback "This uses $P_x-Q_y$, rather than the required cross-partials." :answer/id #uuid "2d1fc223-b2b6-5afb-ae59-69b479c2e240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3} - 8 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704507} {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "80bf97a5-6ce6-5d42-b8fc-2156e3c3c6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - \\frac{2}{3} + 6 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704514} {:answer/feedback "Differentiate the components before subtracting their contributions." :answer/id #uuid "91229cec-f97d-5319-aefc-afc46e97c39d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3 - 2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} + 4 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704517} {:answer/feedback "This keeps only $Q_x$; the $P_y$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "f46d415a-3c11-5411-9821-7831b79865bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "80bf97a5-6ce6-5d42-b8fc-2156e3c3c6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - \\frac{2}{3} + 6 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704514} :answer-field/id #uuid "169e116b-b343-5760-93ad-e9b12d2028a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "391e1a79-9cfc-5601-a5eb-5ea16246c7c8" :question/problem "Given the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(x^{2} + 2 y \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(2 x e^{x y} + y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$, defined where $x+y>0$, evaluate its scalar curl at $(2,1)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the **scalar curl** is $Q_x-P_y$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative. Both cross-partials require the product rule and the chain rule; retain both terms from each product.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(2 x e^{x y} + y^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=2 x y e^{x y} + 2 e^{x y}\\\\\nP_y&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(x^{2} + 2 y \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 y}{x + y} + 2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(2 x y e^{x y} + 2 e^{x y}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{2 y}{x + y} + 2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=2 x y e^{x y} - \\frac{2 y}{x + y} + 2 e^{x y} - 2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate first, then substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(2,1)&=\\left(6 e^{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{2}{3} + 2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - \\frac{2}{3} + 6 e^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This keeps only $-P_y$; the $Q_x$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "1c813780-a9c6-5220-8c8d-e293545a60c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704504} {:answer/feedback "This is the divergence $P_x+Q_y$, not scalar curl." :answer/id #uuid "48b83361-bf34-599d-ae61-4a55ebd3b3ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 - \\frac{18}{e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704510} {:answer/feedback "This uses $Q_y-P_x$, with the differentiation variables interchanged." :answer/id #uuid "b9050478-d197-59e3-9636-d32172d54a8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 + \\frac{18}{e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704520} {:answer/feedback "This keeps only $Q_x$; the $P_y$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "c3799ca6-b60b-52a3-ad43-7ce9121a527b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704521} {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "ec807d70-7246-598e-8cfc-5d02983cb2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 - \\frac{4}{e^{3}} + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "ec807d70-7246-598e-8cfc-5d02983cb2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1 - \\frac{4}{e^{3}} + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704527} :answer-field/id #uuid "9097f5a2-c550-5e87-bad2-3eb4967b1309" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "55e13f49-35b6-5bb3-9376-4a5cd4dbdb64" :question/problem "Given the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- 2 y e^{x y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(2 x \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$, defined where $x+y>0$, evaluate its scalar curl at $(-1,3)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the **scalar curl** is $Q_x-P_y$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative. Both cross-partials require the product rule and the chain rule; retain both terms from each product.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(2 x \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 x}{x + y} + 2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\\\\nP_y&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- 2 y e^{x y}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 x y e^{x y} - 2 e^{x y}\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(\\frac{2 x}{x + y} + 2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)-\\left(- 2 x y e^{x y} - 2 e^{x y}\\right)\\\\\n&=2 x y e^{x y} + \\frac{2 x}{x + y} + 2 e^{x y} + 2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate first, then substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(-1,3)&=\\left(-1 + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{4}{e^{3}}\\right)\\\\\n&=-1 - \\frac{4}{e^{3}} + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704524 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "2984be97-7c3d-51eb-b980-e12ae1c6b9b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 6 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704506} {:answer/feedback "This uses $P_x-Q_y$, rather than the required cross-partials." :answer/id #uuid "45228d4d-5020-5af0-b7ca-27a1331ca582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 e - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704509} {:answer/feedback "This keeps only $Q_x$; the $P_y$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "4ea6611a-6f61-5a1a-8a6e-ae7e39e48f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704511} {:answer/feedback "Differentiate the components before subtracting their contributions." :answer/id #uuid "cfa46d16-8ed0-563c-a120-4b78263b2cca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 3 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704523} {:answer/feedback "This uses $Q_y-P_x$, with the differentiation variables interchanged." :answer/id #uuid "e7e3f045-bdfb-531b-a241-867bec1bd21b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 3 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "2984be97-7c3d-51eb-b980-e12ae1c6b9b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 6 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704506} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ac7f41b-45bd-591b-9193-7fce1b9c84aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e015f6f1-8d43-5562-a834-6dfb83cabb52" :question/problem "Given the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(- 3 y e^{x y}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(2 x \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$, defined where $x+y>0$, evaluate its scalar curl at $(1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the **scalar curl** is $Q_x-P_y$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative. Both cross-partials require the product rule and the chain rule; retain both terms from each product.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(2 x \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 x}{x + y} + 2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\\\\nP_y&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- 3 y e^{x y}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 3 x y e^{x y} - 3 e^{x y}\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(\\frac{2 x}{x + y} + 2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)-\\left(- 3 x y e^{x y} - 3 e^{x y}\\right)\\\\\n&=3 x y e^{x y} + \\frac{2 x}{x + y} + 3 e^{x y} + 2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate first, then substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(1,1)&=\\left(1 + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\\right)-\\left(- 6 e\\right)\\\\\n&=1 + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 6 e\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704525 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This uses $Q_y-P_x$, with the differentiation variables interchanged." :answer/id #uuid "045a7942-b4a2-5646-aa7b-438fef95c201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704501} {:answer/feedback "This reverses the subtraction. Use $Q_x-P_y$." :answer/id #uuid "62b8bb29-bdae-5b0b-af21-2f053c1b8a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + 3 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} + 6 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704513} {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "a09cdf5d-12ec-501c-9521-194959694476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 e^{2} - 3 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704518} {:answer/feedback "This keeps only $Q_x$; the $P_y$ contribution is also required." :answer/id #uuid "b2207378-62d4-5681-bb86-f1b849ae242c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704519} {:answer/feedback "Subtract the cross-partials rather than adding them." :answer/id #uuid "c5ce50ea-4391-5bbd-9a38-e15959028686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 e^{2} + 2 + 3 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y$ from $Q_x$." :answer/id #uuid "a09cdf5d-12ec-501c-9521-194959694476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 e^{2} - 3 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704518} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d9726d3-c821-5583-8b3b-75f10c76de94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e6f2be3b-08db-5231-9240-85ea99ea6097" :question/problem "Given the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(x^{2} + 3 y \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+\\left(- 2 x e^{x y} + y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$, defined where $x+y>0$, evaluate its scalar curl at $(1,2)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the **scalar curl** is $Q_x-P_y$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative. Both cross-partials require the product rule and the chain rule; retain both terms from each product.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- 2 x e^{x y} + y^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 x y e^{x y} - 2 e^{x y}\\\\\nP_y&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(x^{2} + 3 y \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{3 y}{x + y} + 3 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(- 2 x y e^{x y} - 2 e^{x y}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{3 y}{x + y} + 3 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 x y e^{x y} - \\frac{3 y}{x + y} - 2 e^{x y} - 3 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate first, then substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(1,2)&=\\left(- 6 e^{2}\\right)-\\left(2 + 3 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 6 e^{2} - 3 \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} - 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2658b520-4d4f-5f87-a3f5-41a87f2a1fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704568} {:answer/id #uuid "4f09c8e9-b270-500d-9f6e-413f2bc88fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2658b520-4d4f-5f87-a3f5-41a87f2a1fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704568} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a798ddf-8ce0-50e9-8232-dabaf99b3ec3" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the positive $z$-direction everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704566} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc578848-f492-51fc-9455-3574f9b007d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704600} {:answer/id #uuid "eb10d2fb-c34b-5d07-bd3c-1da98c01a500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc578848-f492-51fc-9455-3574f9b007d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704600} :answer-field/id #uuid "202ece59-46ae-5d15-a1e9-100aeb1119e7" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704567} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "170fee62-9e08-544b-aa99-0f26800c5606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704564} {:answer/id #uuid "9097aec1-54ef-520b-81a9-e5077cf088db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "170fee62-9e08-544b-aa99-0f26800c5606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704564} :answer-field/id #uuid "75f2f5c1-73b6-5d5d-9e11-e3c1256e3f53" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae10608-8324-52c6-9a96-3b21b9c2c6ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704561} {:answer/id #uuid "f1235750-568a-50f2-9833-87eaaf9e862e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1235750-568a-50f2-9833-87eaaf9e862e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704607} :answer-field/id #uuid "87ef0278-ed17-5252-9712-b6bace3da512" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02c49169-1d30-5e77-bf66-a061a6d46ef6" :question/problem "![Vector field; arrows share one scale.](images/fb/fbc0162b00e13fece37b6fb1fbd932f2110037f40f84280b8b4a4b1519107c0c.png)\n\nThe diagram shows a vector field $\\mathbf F$ on $\\mathbb R^3$. Its $z$-component is zero and it is independent of $z$. View the $xy$-plane from the positive $z$-axis, so positive $z$ points out of the page. Both planar components are affine functions, and the displayed pattern continues throughout the domain.\n\nAll vectors are horizontal. The horizontal component increases at a constant rate as $y$ increases, and does not change with the other coordinate.\n\nWhich statements are true everywhere? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Imagine a small paddlewheel with its axle parallel to the $z$-axis.\n\nThe horizontal flow is more rightward above a wheel than below it. This contributes a **clockwise** turn.\n\nThe vertical flow is unchanged between the right and left sides of a wheel, so it contributes no rotation.\n\nThe wheel turns **clockwise** everywhere, so $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere. Wrap the fingers of your right hand clockwise: the thumb points into the page, in the **negative $z$-direction**. The field is **not irrotational**.\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ is irrotational: **false**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **true**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the positive $z$-direction everywhere: **false**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **false**.\n\nThe comparison below contrasts unequal sideways pushes with equal pushes.\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186704560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dd63ec3-42d6-598d-aa1e-ee2a4be0eb5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704582} {:answer/id #uuid "93d02919-076a-5308-9802-e0b84654b127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dd63ec3-42d6-598d-aa1e-ee2a4be0eb5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704582} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c4d327c-7401-57ba-8274-fe100189a77f" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d11940e-98d8-5aea-9031-496b25b9853e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704577} {:answer/id #uuid "87c63b5a-2183-5344-9c18-9d6b22ed823c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87c63b5a-2183-5344-9c18-9d6b22ed823c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704590} :answer-field/id #uuid "743ebecf-f21b-535d-a510-110c4e30bb95" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704586} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3810a899-63c2-5190-b00d-f9879c4ae7ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704571} {:answer/id #uuid "4f8b381a-be88-53df-bfd0-cccf90bf8ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3810a899-63c2-5190-b00d-f9879c4ae7ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704571} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5f44069-fa6a-50f1-8025-6167a4cd834d" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the negative $z$-direction everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704598} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d6d945f-f78a-502c-af1e-7a72cb5b7735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704581} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8ec0c4-25a2-5b1b-8e91-b1be43a62067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d6d945f-f78a-502c-af1e-7a72cb5b7735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704581} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb79a8a3-e136-5b01-9090-fb90e6147af6" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186704609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "068c2b18-52fa-523f-bc51-2208bfb11c03" :question/problem "![Vector field; arrows share one scale.](images/62/6265f01b567c086293268e04747e11146dbfa37ad5a1dfbe24f3199eb57ddeff.png)\n\nThe diagram shows a vector field $\\mathbf F$ on $\\mathbb R^3$. Its $z$-component is zero and it is independent of $z$. View the $xy$-plane from the positive $z$-axis, so positive $z$ points out of the page. Both planar components are affine functions, and the displayed pattern continues throughout the domain.\n\nAll vectors are vertical. The vertical component increases at a constant rate as $y$ increases, and does not change with the other coordinate.\n\nWhich statements are true everywhere? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Imagine a small paddlewheel with its axle parallel to the $z$-axis.\n\nThe horizontal flow is unchanged between the upper and lower sides of a wheel, so it contributes no rotation.\n\nThe vertical flow is unchanged between the right and left sides of a wheel, so it contributes no rotation.\n\nChanges of horizontal flow along the horizontal axis and vertical flow along the vertical axis stretch or compress the flow, but add no paddlewheel rotation.\n\nThe wheel does not spin. Thus $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere, and $\\mathbf F$ is **irrotational**. The zero vector has no direction.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the negative $z$-direction everywhere: **false**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **false**.\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ is irrotational: **true**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **true**.\n\nThe comparison below contrasts unequal sideways pushes with equal pushes.\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)"}]}
